    "result_text": "All 275 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required storing telephone numbers as digits-only, returning the stored value in the `telephone` field, and normalizing before the uniqueness check so `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` collide.\n\nThree coordinated changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 relaxed the `telephone` pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9 ()-]*$` so formatted numbers pass Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` instead of being rejected with a 400 before reaching the controller. The DTO is regenerated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `normalizeTelephone()` helper that strips all non-digit characters (`\\D`). It's applied:\n   - in `addOwner` before the duplicate check and before saving (so the stored value is digits-only and the uniqueness comparison sees canonical numbers),\n   - in `updateOwner` for consistency,\n   - inside `isDuplicateOwner`, which now compares telephones digit-for-digit rather than via the whitespace/case `normalize` used for other fields.\n\nThe stored 10-digit value still satisfies the `Owner` entity's `^[0-9]{10}$` constraint on persist. The `Cp11Tests` (`coreStoresDigitsOnly`, `functionalityNormalisedDuplicateRejected`) both pass, and the full suite stays green.",
